{"k":"def","t":"Definite Integration","cls":"12","u":"Calculus","s":[["Fundamentals",[{"q":"Fundamental theorem of calculus","f":"\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx=F(b)-F(a),\\qquad\\frac{d}{dx}\\int_a^xf(t)\\,dt=f(x)"},{"q":"Definite integral as a limit of a sum","f":"\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}h\\sum_{r=1}^nf(a+rh),\\quad h=\\frac{b-a}n","n":"Shortcut: $\\lim\\frac1n\\sum f\\left(\\frac rn\\right)=\\int_0^1f(x)dx$ (replace $\\frac rn\\to x$, $\\frac1n\\to dx$; limits from the range of $\\frac rn$)."}]],["Properties",[{"q":"Basic properties","f":"\\int_a^bf=-\\int_b^af,\\qquad\\int_a^bf=\\int_a^cf+\\int_c^bf,\\qquad\\int_a^bf(x)dx=\\int_a^bf(t)dt"},{"q":"King's property","f":"\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx=\\int_a^bf(a+b-x)\\,dx","n":"Special: $\\int_0^af(x)dx=\\int_0^af(a-x)dx$. Use: $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac{\\sin^nx}{\\sin^nx+\\cos^nx}dx=\\frac\\pi4$."},{"q":"Even and odd functions","f":"\\int_{-a}^af(x)\\,dx=\\begin{cases}2\\int_0^af(x)dx,&f\\ \\text{even}\\\\0,&f\\ \\text{odd}\\end{cases}","n":"General: $\\int_{-a}^af(x)dx=\\int_0^a[f(x)+f(-x)]dx$."},{"q":"Doubling property","f":"\\int_0^{2a}f(x)\\,dx=\\begin{cases}2\\int_0^af(x)dx,&f(2a-x)=f(x)\\\\0,&f(2a-x)=-f(x)\\end{cases}"},{"q":"Periodic function","f":"\\int_0^{nT}f(x)\\,dx=n\\int_0^Tf(x)\\,dx,\\qquad\\int_a^{a+T}f(x)\\,dx=\\int_0^Tf(x)\\,dx","n":"$\\int_{a+nT}^{b+nT}f=\\int_a^bf$."},{"q":"$xf(\\sin x)$ result","f":"\\int_0^\\pi xf(\\sin x)\\,dx=\\frac\\pi2\\int_0^\\pi f(\\sin x)\\,dx","d":"Apply King's rule: $I=\\int_0^\\pi(\\pi-x)f(\\sin x)dx$; add the two forms."},{"q":"Bounds on integrals","f":"m(b-a)\\le\\int_a^bf\\le M(b-a);\\qquad\\left|\\int_a^bf\\right|\\le\\int_a^b|f|","n":"$f\\le g$ on $[a,b]\\Rightarrow\\int f\\le\\int g$."},{"q":"King's rule general use with sum","f":"I=\\int_a^b\\frac{f(x)}{f(x)+f(a+b-x)}dx=\\frac{b-a}2"},{"q":"Integral over symmetric interval of $\\frac{f(x)}{1+a^x}$","f":"\\int_{-c}^c\\frac{f(x)}{1+a^x}dx=\\int_0^cf(x)\\,dx\\quad(f\\ \\text{even})"},{"q":"Integral of an odd function times even","f":"\\int_{-a}^a(\\text{odd})\\,dx=0;\\quad\\text{e.g. }\\int_{-1}^1x^3\\cos x\\,dx=0"},{"q":"Integral of periodic function over shifted period","f":"\\int_a^{a+nT}f(x)\\,dx=n\\int_0^Tf(x)\\,dx"},{"q":"Integrals of $|\\sin x|$, $|\\cos x|$","f":"\\int_0^{n\\pi}|\\sin x|\\,dx=2n,\\qquad\\int_0^{n\\pi}|\\cos x|\\,dx=2n"},{"q":"Integral of $f$ and $f^{-1}$","f":"\\int_0^af(x)\\,dx+\\int_0^{f(a)}f^{-1}(y)\\,dy=af(a)\\quad(f(0)=0,\\ f\\ \\text{increasing})"}]],["Standard results",[{"q":"Wallis' formula","f":"\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^nx\\,dx=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos^nx\\,dx=\\frac{(n-1)(n-3)\\cdots}{n(n-2)\\cdots}\\times\\begin{cases}\\frac\\pi2,&n\\ \\text{even}\\\\1,&n\\ \\text{odd}\\end{cases}"},{"q":"Wallis for $\\sin^m x\\cos^n x$","f":"\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^mx\\cos^nx\\,dx=\\frac{[(m-1)(m-3)\\cdots][(n-1)(n-3)\\cdots]}{(m+n)(m+n-2)\\cdots}\\times\\left(\\tfrac\\pi2\\ \\text{if } m,n\\ \\text{both even, else }1\\right)"},{"q":"Log-sine integral","f":"\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\ln\\sin x\\,dx=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\ln\\cos x\\,dx=-\\frac\\pi2\\ln2","d":"Add the two equal forms: $2I=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\ln\\frac{\\sin2x}2dx$; substitute $2x=t$ to get $2I=I-\\frac\\pi2\\ln2$."},{"q":"Gamma-type integral","f":"\\int_0^\\infty x^ne^{-x}\\,dx=n!,\\qquad\\int_0^\\infty e^{-ax}dx=\\frac1a","n":"$\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x^2}dx=\\frac{\\sqrt\\pi}2$."},{"q":"Greatest integer in integrals","f":"\\int_0^n[x]\\,dx=\\frac{n(n-1)}2,\\qquad\\int_0^n\\{x\\}\\,dx=\\frac n2","n":"Split at the integers where $[\\,]$ jumps."},{"q":"Integrals with $|\\,|$ or $\\max/\\min$","f":"\\text{split the interval where the inside changes sign}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac{dx}{a^2\\cos^2x+b^2\\sin^2x}$","f":"\\frac\\pi{2ab}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^{\\pi}\\frac{x\\,dx}{1+\\sin x}$, $\\int_0^\\pi\\frac{x\\sin x}{1+\\cos^2x}dx$","f":"\\pi;\\qquad\\frac{\\pi^2}4"},{"q":"$\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac{\\sqrt{\\sin x}}{\\sqrt{\\sin x}+\\sqrt{\\cos x}}dx$","f":"\\frac\\pi4"},{"q":"$\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln x}{1-x}dx$ and $\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln x}{1+x}dx$","f":"-\\frac{\\pi^2}6;\\qquad-\\frac{\\pi^2}{12}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^\\infty\\frac{\\sin x}xdx$ and $\\int_0^\\infty\\frac{dx}{1+x^2}$","f":"\\frac\\pi2;\\qquad\\frac\\pi2"},{"q":"$\\int_0^1x^m(1-x)^ndx$ (Beta)","f":"\\frac{m!\\,n!}{(m+n+1)!}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^\\pi\\ln(1+\\cos x)\\,dx$ and $\\int_0^\\pi x\\ln\\sin x\\,dx$","f":"-\\pi\\ln2;\\qquad-\\frac{\\pi^2}2\\ln2"},{"q":"Integrals of $e^{-x}$ with powers","f":"\\int_0^\\infty x^ne^{-ax}dx=\\frac{n!}{a^{n+1}}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\sin^mx\\cos^nx\\,dx$","f":"0\\ \\text{if } m \\text{ or } n \\text{ odd}"},{"q":"$\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^n x\\,dx$ recurrence","f":"I_n=\\frac{n-1}nI_{n-2}"},{"q":"Integrals with $[x]$ and $\\{x\\}$ (more)","f":"\\int_0^n\\{x\\}^2dx=\\frac n3;\\qquad\\int_0^n x[x]\\,dx=\\frac{n(n-1)(4n+1)}{12}","n":"Split at the integers: on $[k,k+1)$, $[x]=k$."}]],["Leibniz rule",[{"q":"Differentiating an integral with variable limits","f":"\\frac d{dx}\\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)}f(t)\\,dt=f(\\psi(x))\\psi'(x)-f(\\phi(x))\\phi'(x)"},{"q":"Differentiation under the integral sign","f":"\\frac d{d\\alpha}\\int_a^bf(x,\\alpha)\\,dx=\\int_a^b\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial\\alpha}dx"},{"q":"Limit of an integral ratio","f":"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\int_0^xf(t)dt}{x}=f(0)\\quad(\\text{L'Hôpital + Leibniz})"},{"q":"$F(x)=\\int_0^xf(t)dt$ properties","f":"f\\ \\text{odd}\\Rightarrow F\\ \\text{even};\\quad f\\ \\text{even}\\Rightarrow F\\ \\text{odd};\\quad f\\ \\text{periodic with zero mean}\\Rightarrow F\\ \\text{periodic}"}]],["Common results",[{"q":"Classic King's results","f":"\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac{dx}{1+\\tan^nx}=\\frac\\pi4,\\qquad\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\ln(1+\\tan x)\\,dx=\\frac\\pi8\\ln2","n":"$\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln(1+x)}{1+x^2}dx=\\frac\\pi8\\ln2$ (put $x=\\tan\\theta$)."},{"q":"Inverse-function integral","f":"\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx+\\int_{f(a)}^{f(b)}f^{-1}(y)\\,dy=bf(b)-af(a)"},{"q":"Mean value of a function","f":"\\bar f=\\frac1{b-a}\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx"},{"q":"Useful definite values","f":"\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^2x\\,dx=\\frac\\pi4,\\qquad\\int_0^\\pi\\sin x\\,dx=2,\\qquad\\int_0^1\\frac{dx}{1+x^2}=\\frac\\pi4"},{"q":"Estimation with inequalities","f":"\\frac2\\pi x\\le\\sin x\\le x\\Rightarrow\\int\\ \\text{bounds};\\qquad\\int_0^1e^{x^2}dx\\in(1,e)"},{"q":"Integral equation $f(x)=g(x)+\\int_a^b f(t)\\,dt$","f":"\\text{let } k=\\int_a^bf(t)dt,\\ \\text{then } f=g+k;\\ \\text{integrate to find } k"},{"q":"Integral equation with variable limit","f":"f(x)=g(x)+\\int_0^xf(t)dt\\Rightarrow f'=g'+f\\ \\ (\\text{linear DE})"},{"q":"Sum $\\lim\\sum\\frac n{n^2+r^2}$ / $\\lim\\sum\\frac1{\\sqrt{n^2-r^2}}$","f":"\\int_0^1\\frac{dx}{1+x^2}=\\frac\\pi4;\\qquad\\int_0^1\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}=\\frac\\pi2"},{"q":"Limit of product as integral","f":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left(\\prod_{r=1}^n\\left(1+\\frac rn\\right)\\right)^{1/n}=\\frac4e","d":"Take log: $\\frac1n\\sum\\ln(1+\\frac rn)\\to\\int_0^1\\ln(1+x)dx=2\\ln2-1$."}]],["If this type comes, solve like this",[{"q":"If the limits are symmetric ($-a$ to $a$) and the integrand looks ugly","f":"\\int_{-a}^af(x)dx=\\int_0^a[f(x)+f(-x)]dx;\\qquad\\frac{g(x)}{1+e^{h(x)}}\\ \\text{with } h \\text{ odd}\\Rightarrow\\int_0^ag","n":"Pair $f(x)$ with $f(-x)$: $\\frac1{1+e^{u}}+\\frac1{1+e^{-u}}=1$. Odd parts vanish ($\\ln(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1})$ is odd).","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 44 times"},{"q":"If the integrand is $\\frac{f(x)}{f(x)+f(a+b-x)}$ or has $\\sin^n$ vs $\\cos^n$","f":"\\int_a^bf(x)dx=\\int_a^bf(a+b-x)dx\\ \\Rightarrow\\ 2I=\\int_a^b1\\,dx","n":"Also for $x\\cdot g(\\sin x)$ on $[0,\\pi]$: $I=\\frac\\pi2\\int g$. Then finish the remaining integral with $t=\\tan^2x$ or $t=\\sin^2x$.","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 34 times"},{"q":"If $[x]$, $\\{x\\}$, $\\min/\\max$ of greatest-integer pieces appear","f":"\\text{split at points where the inside crosses integers; on each piece the integrand is simple}","n":"For $[x^2]$ on $[0,2.4]$: breaks at $1,\\sqrt2,\\sqrt3,2,\\sqrt5$. For $\\int\\frac{[x]e^{[x]}}{e^{x-1}}$: sum over unit intervals → a GP.","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 48 times"},{"q":"If it is $\\lim\\sum\\frac{1}{n}f\\left(\\frac kn\\right)$ in disguise","f":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac1n\\sum_{k=1}^nf\\left(\\frac kn\\right)=\\int_0^1f(x)dx","n":"Pull out $\\frac1n$ and write the rest in $\\frac kn$; e.g. $\\frac{n^3}{(n^2+k^2)(n^2+3k^2)}=\\frac1n\\cdot\\frac{1}{(1+x^2)(1+3x^2)}$.","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 17 times"},{"q":"If $f$ is defined by an integral equation ($f(x)=g(x)+\\int_0^x\\ldots$ or $+\\int_a^b\\ldots f(t)dt$)","f":"\\text{variable limit: differentiate (Leibniz) to get a DE};\\quad\\text{constant limits: the integral is a constant } k","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 37 times"},{"q":"If a limit contains an integral with variable limit","f":"\\frac{d}{dx}\\int_a^{g(x)}h(t)dt=h(g(x))g'(x);\\ \\text{use L'Hôpital}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 12 times"},{"q":"If integration by parts relates $\\int xF'$, $\\int x^2F''$","f":"\\int_a^bxF'\\,dx=[xF]_a^b-\\int_a^bF\\,dx","p":"2 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 22 times"},{"q":"If it is $\\int\\frac{t^4+1}{t^6+1}$ or $\\int\\frac{\\sqrt{x(\\ldots)}}{\\ldots}$ with hidden factoring","f":"t^6+1=(t^2+1)(t^4-t^2+1)\\Rightarrow\\frac{t^4+1}{t^6+1}=\\frac1{t^2+1}+\\frac{t^2}{t^6+1}","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 18 times"},{"q":"If it is a Beta-type $\\int_0^1x^{m-1}(1-x)^{n-1}$","f":"I(m,n)=\\frac{(m-1)!(n-1)!}{(m+n-1)!},\\quad I(m,n)=I(n,m)","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 6 times"},{"q":"If it asks extrema/sign of $\\int_{-1}^xg(t)dt$ with a factored $g$","f":"F'(x)=g(x):\\ \\text{sign changes only at odd-multiplicity zeros}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 6 times"},{"q":"If it is $\\int\\frac{dx}{a+b\\sin x+c\\cos x}$ on $[0,\\frac\\pi2]$","f":"t=\\tan\\tfrac x2\\Rightarrow\\int_0^1\\frac{2\\,dt}{(a-c)t^2+2bt+(a+c)}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 5 times"},{"q":"If reduction / recurrence of $\\int\\cot^nx$ or $\\tan^nx$","f":"I_n+I_{n-2}=\\frac{1}{n-1}\\left[\\ldots\\right]\\ \\ (\\text{use } \\cot^2=\\csc^2-1)","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 5 times"},{"q":"If bounds or a periodic-like relation $f(x)+f(x+k)=n$ are given","f":"f(x+2k)=f(x)\\Rightarrow\\text{period } 2k;\\ \\int_0^{2k}f=nk","p":"2 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 9 times"},{"q":"If $\\cot^{-1}$ of a quadratic is integrated","f":"\\cot^{-1}(1-x+x^2)=\\tan^{-1}x+\\tan^{-1}(1-x)\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\text{use King's rule}","p":"2 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 4 times"}]]]}